# Decide the site's capabilities: search and read over the knowledge base

## Step

The finish line says every MCP tool is a capability. Decide which: the recommendation is two, `search` (query to ranked matches over the resources and skills, with the same token-overlap ranking `catalog.ts` already has) and `read` (a resource id to its text), defined with `defineCapability` inside `apps/mischief` and projected with `toToolkit` and `toHttpApi`, so `/openapi.json` and the API catalog come for free. Decide whether the code-mode `execute` tool is exposed too (recommendation: no, on day one; there is nothing to compose) and whether `greet` survives anywhere (recommendation: no).

## Result (2026-09-21)

Joel's call: three capabilities. `search` and `read` as recommended, and code mode's `execute` too, on day one. `greet` stays dead. Consequence: the subprocess `Sandbox` cannot run in a Worker, so `execute` needs a Worker-side `Sandbox` layer; that is the new research step [research-worker-sandbox](./research-worker-sandbox.svx), and the prototype grows `search`, `read`, and `execute` once it lands.
